ipatool-store-proof is a separate Linux executable. Its source is distributed
under the GNU Library General Public License version 2; see COPYING-LGPLv2.

internal/adi and internal/androidlib were adapted from:
  https://github.com/hpidcock/ap
  commit e690795d17446ddabe348f890c130a2280900430
  internal/anisette/local/{adi,androidlib}

Those packages are a Go port of the ADI wrapper and Android library loader from:
  https://github.com/Dadoum/Provision
  Copyright (c) 2023, Dadoum
  GNU Library General Public License version 2

Local modifications include the import path, provenance comments and the
Store-specific command, provisioning protocol and verified library installer.
The helper uses machine scope -1 and Apple's Store provisioning endpoint.
It does not use the AuthKit/GrandSlam provisioning workflow (scope -2).

Apple libraries are not included. Setup extracts verified libraries from
Apple's public Apple Music APK. They remain Apple's proprietary software.

The main ipatool executable remains a separate program and communicates with
this helper through bounded JSON on stdin/stdout; it does not link these packages.
